/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 45 0 R
/T (Assume binary units: 4 GiB / 4 KiB = 2^32 / 2^12 = 1,048,576 blocks. To reach the last block: contiguous allocation calculates its address in O\(1\), then reads the data block \(one data read\); linked allocation may read/traverse 1,048,575 pointers plus the target block \(up to 1,048,576 block reads\); FAT in RAM performs about 1,048,575 memory lookups plus one data read; inode indexing for this file reaches the last block through double-indirect pointers, requiring two index-block reads plus the data read \(about 3 cold reads\).)
/E (Assume binary units: 4 GiB / 4 KiB = 2^32 / 2^12 = 1,048,576 blocks. To reach the last block: contiguous allocation calculates its address in O\(1\), then reads the data block \(one data read\); linked allocation may read/traverse 1,048,575 pointers plus the target block \(up to 1,048,576 block reads\); FAT in RAM performs about 1,048,575 memory lookups plus one data read; inode indexing for this file reaches the last block through double-indirect pointers, requiring two index-block reads plus the data read \(about 3 cold reads\).)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
