<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 49 0 R
/T (Drivers translate OS operations into hardware commands and handle interrupts/errors. The block-device interface exposes addressable blocks. Buffering handles speed differences and combines I/O; caching retains hot blocks in memory; spooling queues work for serial processing. These mechanisms improve throughput and responsiveness.)
/E (Drivers translate OS operations into hardware commands and handle interrupts/errors. The block-device interface exposes addressable blocks. Buffering handles speed differences and combines I/O; caching retains hot blocks in memory; spooling queues work for serial processing. These mechanisms improve throughput and responsiveness.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [13]
>>
