699 0 obj
<<
/Title (A write may update data, allocation metadata and directory entries. Power loss between updates can leave inconsistent metadata or orphaned blocks. Journaling records intended changes and replays committed transactions after reboot. CoW writes changed blocks elsewhere and switches metadata roots atomically, preserving an older consistent tree if interrupted. ext4 data=journal journals data and metadata \(more writes\); ordered journals metadata and writes associated data before metadata commit \(common default\); writeback journals metadata without ordering data first, so stale data may appear after a crash. Neither replaces backups.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 681 0 R
>>
endobj
